ng female protagonist connected to nature, and the follies of war.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw130","target":"aw217","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"The film's epic scale, morally complex characters, and depiction of conflict in a tumultuous period of Japanese history echo the style and tone of Kurosawa's jidaigeki masterpieces.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw177","target":"aw130","type":"influenced","label":"Influenced","note":"Miyazaki himself has described 'Princess Mononoke' as a more complex and cynical re-examination of the themes he first explored in Nausicaä, particularly the irresolvable conflict between human industry and the natural world.","direction":"incoming"}],"lineage":{"influenced_by":["aw130","aw130","aw130","aw130"],"influences":["aw130"]},"stats":{"total_connected":4,"influences_count":2,"influenced_count":3,"filter":"all","vault_count":0,"beyond_count":4}}